# Line-ending policy.
#
# This file exists because it was missing, and the cost was concrete: with
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git normalised CRLF->LF *inside binary files*
# on commit, and every PNG in app/android was committed corrupt. A PNG's
# 8-byte signature is 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A -- it contains \r\n precisely so
# that this damage is detectable -- and all 26 of them were stored as
# 89 50 4E 47 0A 1A 0A, with every other 0D0A in the image data stripped too.
# That is not reversible: nothing records which 0A bytes used to be 0D0A.
#
# aapt2 rejects them ("file failed to compile"), so no APK could be built from
# a clean checkout. It went unnoticed because local builds reused cached
# compiled resources from before the corruption.
#
# Text files get normalised in the repo and checked out native.
* text=auto

# Binary: never touched, never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.bin  binary
*.apk  binary
*.jks  binary
*.keystore binary
*.ttf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.pdf  binary

# Scripts that must keep LF or they break the tool reading them: a shebang
# followed by \r makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "python3\r",
# and gradlew is run by sh in CI.
*.sh      text eol=lf
gradlew   text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers that must keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
